  "title": "Eye trauma: is the globe OPEN?",
  "lines": [
   "look for: PEAKED pupil (in EVERY trauma) · Seidel sign · 360° subconjunctival hemorrhage · dark tissue at the limbus (extruded uvea) · depth of the wound · shallow chamber",
   "also: orbital rim pain or step-off · air under the skin · lid lacerations (full thickness? tear duct?) · forehead and cheek sensation (V1, V2) · eye movements · proptosis or sunken eye",
   "ONLY ophthalmologists prescribe topical steroids"
  ]
